    "result_text": "All 16 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed telephone handling so numbers are stored and compared in E.164 form.\n\n**Core logic \u2014 `ValidateOwnerFields.java`** (`rest/function/owner/`): replaced the old \"strip to exactly 10 digits\" `normalizeTelephone` with an E.164 conversion (`toE164`):\n- Strips spaces, dashes, and brackets.\n- If a leading `+` is present, keeps it and the country code as-is.\n- Otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits.\n- Requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, else the request is rejected (`telephone` error \u2192 400).\n\nSo `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678`, `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456`, and `12` is rejected.\n\n**Duplicate detection \u2014 unchanged code, now correct by construction:** `RejectDuplicateTelephone` compares stored `telephone` values, which are now E.164, so national and international spellings of the same number collide (Cp03).\n\n**Validation constraints updated to accept the new stored form** (otherwise the E.164 value would be rejected downstream):\n- `openapi.yml` telephone pattern `^[0-9]*$` \u2192 `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` (the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` is validated after normalization).\n- `Owner.java` entity: dropped `@Digits`, changed `@Pattern` from `^[0-9]{10}$` to `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` (validated on JPA persist).\n\nThe full suite (16 tests, including the new Cp02/Cp03/Cp08 telephone tests) is green.",
